    "original": "To evaluate post-hoc refinement in high-granularity regimes, we introduce two diagnostics: topic dispersion, which measures distributional bal-ance and penalises mega-topics more heavily than niche ones, and topic discriminability, which mea-sures how well a topic’s representation aligns with its assigned documents relative to non-assigned documents. Across two patent corpora and a legal corpus, we find that 83% of high-similarity topic pairs are rejected as non-redundant by the LLM. EGIM improves topic discriminability by 25–55% over an iterative LLM baseline while preserving over 94% of original topic dispersion across all three corpora, compared to 34–88% for the base-line.",
